@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`createTaskList` in `src/domain/list.ts` builds tasks via `createTask`, `renameTask` and `addTag`, which cannot fail. Domain code must return a `Result`, never throw, and not read the clock.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** validate in the domain, with clear messages; reject before any state changes.
+
+**Non-Goals:** normalizing tags, changing the `untag` or lookup behavior, UI changes.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Add `invalid-input` to `TodoErrorCode`.
+- Add pure validators in `task.ts` (`validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag`) returning `Result`; titles are trimmed first, as the list already does, and the 120 limit applies to the trimmed title.
+- In `list.ts`, validate at the start of `add`, `rename` and `tag`, before the duplicate check and before consuming an id, so nothing changes on rejection. For `rename` and `tag`, an unknown task still reports `not-found` first only if the input is valid; input validation runs first.
+- Priority is checked at runtime against `PRIORITIES`, since screens may pass untyped values.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+Existing callers passing a blank title now get an error rather than a blank task; this is the intent.
