+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so empty, huge or malformed titles, unknown priorities and tags with spaces end up in the list.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `add`, `rename` and `tag` reject invalid input with a result error that says what is wrong; the list is left unchanged.
+- Invalid: a title empty or only spaces; a title over 120 characters (after trimming); a priority other than `low`, `normal`, `high`; a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+- New error code `invalid-input`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-input-validation`: what input `add`, `rename` and `tag` accept and how they reject the rest.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `src/domain/result.ts` (new error code), tests in `test/`. No new dependency; the public API gains only the `invalid-input` code.
